{"id":26281,"path":"/vocabulary/a1/opposite-adjectives-for-describing-people-and-things-a1-english-vocabulary/","parentId":26178,"order":40,"section":"vocabulary","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Opposite adjectives for describing people and things – A1 English Vocabulary","seo":{"title":"Opposite adjectives for describing people and things – A1 English Vocabulary - Test-English","description":"Learn opposite adjectives to describe people and things with our A1 vocabulary lesson. It includes pictures, examples, exercises and games!","image":"/media/uploads/A1-English-Vocabulary_Adjectives-describing-people-things.jpg"},"modified":"2023-10-11T08:14:19","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h2>Opposite adjectives for describing people and things</h2> <p>In this elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">vocabulary</a> lesson about Opposite Adjectives, you will learn basic opposite adjectives used for describing people and things. Check the explanation and do the exercises.</p> <hr> <h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct opposite adjective to complete each sentence.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"934\"></div>","<h2>Opposite adjectives for describing people and things</h2> <h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct opposite adjective for each gap.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"935\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h2>Opposite adjectives for describing people and things</h2> <h5>Fill in each gap with the correct opposite adjective.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"936\"></div>","<h2>Opposite adjectives for describing people and things</h2> <h3>Exercise 4</h3> <h5>Match the sentences/pictures with the terms.</h5> <p></p> <h6>Reload the page to play again. Here’s a link to our <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/es/820309095/opposite-adjectives-for-describing-people-and-things-a1-vocabulary-flash-cards/?i=4i1uip&amp;x=1jqt\">Quizlet study set</a> about Opposite adjectives for describing people and things.</h6>"],"explanation":"<h2>Opposite Adjectives for Describing People &amp; Things</h2> <p>In this A1 Elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">Vocabulary</a> Lesson, you will discover many opposite adjectives that you can use to describe people and things. Check the following pictures and sentence examples.</p> <h3>Opposite Adjectives Used to Describe People</h3> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-26341\" src=\"/media/uploads/Adjectives-describing-people_A1-vocabulary.png\" alt=\"Comparison chart of opposite adjectives describing people for A1 English learners.\" width=\"500\" height=\"624\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h4>Example Sentences</h4> <ul class=\"vocab-ex\"> <li>I’m <span class=\"numPink\">1</span> <strong><span>happy</span></strong> when I spend time with my family, and I’m <span class=\"numPink\">2</span> <span><strong>sad</strong></span> when I fail an exam.</li> <li>Tom is <span class=\"numPink\">3</span> <span><strong>tall</strong></span>; he is 6 feet 3 inches. Peter is <span class=\"numPink\">4</span> <span><strong>short</strong></span>; he is 5 feet 4 inches.</li> <li>I’m <span class=\"numPink\">5</span> <span><strong>young</strong></span>; I’m 26. However, my granddad is very <span class=\"numPink\">6</span> <span><strong>old</strong></span>; he is 92.</li> <li>Carlos is very <span class=\"numPink\">7</span> <span><strong>strong</strong></span>; he goes to the gym every day. Richard is <span class=\"numPink\">8</span> <span><strong>weak</strong></span>, he hardly ever does exercise.</li> <li>David is <span class=\"numPink\">9</span> <span><strong>fat</strong></span>; he eats a lot. Maria is <span class=\"numPink\">10</span> <span><strong>thin</strong></span>; she needs to eat more.</li> <li>She is a <span class=\"numPink\">11</span> <span><strong>beautiful</strong></span> model, but her cousin is very <span class=\"numPink\">12</span> <span><strong>ugly</strong></span>.</li> </ul> <h3>Opposite Adjectives Used to Describe Things</h3> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-26342\" src=\"/media/uploads/Adjectives-describing-things_A1-vocabulary.png\" alt=\"Opposite adjectives describing objects visual guide for A1 English vocabulary.\" width=\"500\" height=\"1136\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h4>Example sentences</h4> <ul class=\"vocab-ex\"> <li>The elephant is <span class=\"numPink\">1</span> <strong><span>big</span></strong>, and the mosquito is <span class=\"numPink\">2</span> <span><strong>small</strong></span>.</li> <li>The coffee is <span class=\"numPink\">3</span> <span><strong>hot</strong></span>, and the sodas are <span class=\"numPink\">4</span> <span><strong>cold</strong></span>.</li> <li>The tortoise is <span class=\"numPink\">5</span> <span><strong>slow</strong></span>, and the car is <span class=\"numPink\">6</span> <span><strong>fast</strong></span>.</li> <li>Vegetables and eggs are <span class=\"numPink\">7</span> <span><strong>good</strong></span> for you, and fast food and smoking are <span class=\"numPink\">8</span> <span><strong>bad</strong></span>.</li> <li>The rock is very <span class=\"numPink\">9</span> <span><strong>heavy</strong></span>, and the feather is <span class=\"numPink\">10</span> <span><strong>light</strong></span>.</li> <li>The rocks are <span class=\"numPink\">11</span> <span><strong>hard</strong></span>, and the cushions are <span class=\"numPink\">12</span> <span><strong>soft</strong></span>.</li> <li>The first pencil is <span class=\"numPink\">13</span> <span><strong>thick</strong></span>, and the second pencil is <span class=\"numPink\">14</span> <span><strong>thin</strong></span>.</li> <li>The first glass is <span class=\"numPink\">15</span> <span><strong>full</strong></span> and the second glass is <span class=\"numPink\">16</span> <span><strong>empty</strong></span>.</li> <li>The first bathroom is <span class=\"numPink\">17</span> <span><strong>clean</strong></span>, and the second bathroom is <span class=\"numPink\">18</span> <span><strong>dirty</strong></span>.</li> <li>The first room is <span class=\"numPink\">19</span> <span><strong>dim</strong></span>, there is no light. The second room is <span class=\"numPink\">20</span> <span><strong>bright</strong></span>.</li> <li>The car is <span class=\"numPink\">21</span> <span><strong>expensive</strong></span>; it costs a lot of money. The scooter is <span class=\"numPink\">22</span> <span><strong>cheap</strong></span>.</li> <li>The purple nails are <span class=\"numPink\">23</span> <span><strong>long</strong></span>, but the nails in the second picture are <span class=\"numPink\">24</span> <span><strong>short</strong></span>.</li> </ul> <h3>Listen &amp; Practice: Vocabulary with Pronunciation</h3> <p>Here’s a video to help you review the vocabulary from this lesson and improve your pronunciation.</p> <div class=\"video-container\"> <div class=\"embed-container\"><div data-youtube=\"4UWyUWkMTi0\"></div></div> </div> <div class=\"separator-dots\"><span>Flashcards</span></div> <p>After completing the exercises in this lesson on Opposite Adjective, you can use the unit’s <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/820309095\">Vocabulary Flashcards</a> to revise and help you memorize the terms.</p>","quizzes":[{"id":934,"questions":[{"id":7887,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Adam is tall, but Axel is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["sad","small","bad","slow","short","cold","strong","ugly","thin","old"]}]},{"id":7888,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Some days I'm happy, and some days I'm <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["strong","cold","bad","sad","slow","old","small","thin","ugly","short"]}]},{"id":7889,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My uncle is fat, but my cousin is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["short","cold","small","old","ugly","bad","thin","slow","sad","strong"]}]},{"id":7890,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I am weak, but my brother is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["thin","old","small","cold","slow","short","ugly","sad","bad","strong"]}]},{"id":7891,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My history teacher is young, but my math teacher is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["short","slow","bad","old","sad","thin","ugly","small","cold","strong"]}]},{"id":7892,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Their garden is beautiful, but their house is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["bad","short","cold","strong","thin","sad","small","ugly","old","slow"]}]},{"id":7893,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They have a big house, but their car is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["short","small","sad","strong","cold","bad","old","ugly","slow","thin"]}]},{"id":7894,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>It was hot yesterday, but today it's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["old","slow","ugly","bad","thin","short","small","strong","cold","sad"]}]},{"id":7895,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The rabbit is fast, but the turtle is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["thin","strong","sad","small","cold","ugly","bad","old","slow","short"]}]},{"id":7896,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Her cooking is usually good, but today's food is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["bad","sad","ugly","old","cold","slow","short","strong","small","thin"]}]}]},{"id":935,"questions":[{"id":7897,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>My glass was full, but now it's _____.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":13954,"html":"light"},{"id":13955,"html":"soft"},{"id":13956,"html":"thick"},{"id":13957,"html":"empty"},{"id":13958,"html":"dirty"},{"id":13959,"html":"bright"},{"id":13960,"html":"expensive"},{"id":13961,"html":"long"},{"id":13962,"html":"fast"},{"id":13963,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7898,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>My backpack is heavy, and your backpack is _____.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":13964,"html":"light"},{"id":13965,"html":"soft"},{"id":13966,"html":"thick"},{"id":13967,"html":"empty"},{"id":13968,"html":"dirty"},{"id":13969,"html":"bright"},{"id":13970,"html":"expensive"},{"id":13971,"html":"long"},{"id":13972,"html":"fast"},{"id":13973,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7899,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The rooms downstairs are dim, but the rooms upstairs are _____.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":13974,"html":"light"},{"id":13975,"html":"soft"},{"id":13976,"html":"thick"},{"id":13977,"html":"empty"},{"id":13978,"html":"dirty"},{"id":13979,"html":"bright"},{"id":13980,"html":"expensive"},{"id":13981,"html":"long"},{"id":13982,"html":"fast"},{"id":13983,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7900,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>A koala is slow, and a kangaroo is _____.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":13984,"html":"light"},{"id":13985,"html":"soft"},{"id":13986,"html":"thick"},{"id":13987,"html":"empty"},{"id":13988,"html":"dirty"},{"id":13989,"html":"bright"},{"id":13990,"html":"expensive"},{"id":13991,"html":"long"},{"id":13992,"html":"fast"},{"id":13993,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7901,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>This restaurant was cheap in the past, but now it's _____.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":13994,"html":"light"},{"id":13995,"html":"soft"},{"id":13996,"html":"thick"},{"id":13997,"html":"empty"},{"id":13998,"html":"dirty"},{"id":13999,"html":"bright"},{"id":14000,"html":"expensive"},{"id":14001,"html":"long"},{"id":14002,"html":"fast"},{"id":14003,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7902,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>This bed is hard. I want a _____ bed.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":14004,"html":"light"},{"id":14005,"html":"soft"},{"id":14006,"html":"thick"},{"id":14007,"html":"empty"},{"id":14008,"html":"dirty"},{"id":14009,"html":"bright"},{"id":14010,"html":"expensive"},{"id":14011,"html":"long"},{"id":14012,"html":"fast"},{"id":14013,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7903,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>This line is very thin. You need to draw a _____ line.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":14014,"html":"light"},{"id":14015,"html":"soft"},{"id":14016,"html":"thick"},{"id":14017,"html":"empty"},{"id":14018,"html":"dirty"},{"id":14019,"html":"bright"},{"id":14020,"html":"expensive"},{"id":14021,"html":"long"},{"id":14022,"html":"fast"},{"id":14023,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7904,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Are these clothes clean or _____?</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":14024,"html":"light"},{"id":14025,"html":"soft"},{"id":14026,"html":"thick"},{"id":14027,"html":"empty"},{"id":14028,"html":"dirty"},{"id":14029,"html":"bright"},{"id":14030,"html":"expensive"},{"id":14031,"html":"long"},{"id":14032,"html":"fast"},{"id":14033,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7905,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Your soup is cold, but my soup is _____.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":14034,"html":"light"},{"id":14035,"html":"soft"},{"id":14036,"html":"thick"},{"id":14037,"html":"empty"},{"id":14038,"html":"dirty"},{"id":14039,"html":"bright"},{"id":14040,"html":"expensive"},{"id":14041,"html":"long"},{"id":14042,"html":"fast"},{"id":14043,"html":"hot"}]},{"id":7906,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I don't like _____ films, I prefer short films.</div>","display":"dropdown","choices":[{"id":14044,"html":"light"},{"id":14045,"html":"soft"},{"id":14046,"html":"thick"},{"id":14047,"html":"empty"},{"id":14048,"html":"dirty"},{"id":14049,"html":"bright"},{"id":14050,"html":"expensive"},{"id":14051,"html":"long"},{"id":14052,"html":"fast"},{"id":14053,"html":"hot"}]}]},{"id":936,"questions":[{"id":7907,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The rock is hard, but the pillow is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7908,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The steak is thick, but the paper is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7909,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The cup was full of water, but now it's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7910,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The room was clean, but now it's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7911,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The sun is bright, but the moon is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7912,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This handbag is expensive, but that handbag is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7913,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Is it a long story or a <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> story?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7914,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He's normally happy, but today he looks <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7915,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>His aunt is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>, but his uncle is fat.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":7916,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The new student is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>, but the teacher is old.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}